# Trivy ignore list: advisories that no relock can fix yet. Trivy reads only this file
# (.trivyignore in the directory it runs from) unless it is passed another, and ci.yml's
# `security` job passes none, so these plain-format entries apply REPO-WIDE, to every
# manifest a scan from the root reads: the root poetry.lock, docker/imagegen's poetry.lock
# and docker/imagegen/requirements-runtime.txt (the facade runtime, where the setuptools and
# torch entries below also apply). Trivy's pip analyzer matches only files named
# requirements.txt, so the `security` job reads that runtime lock through
# TRIVY_FILE_PATTERNS='pip:requirements-runtime\.txt'; pass the same --file-patterns to a
# local scan. A `.trivyignore.yaml` would never be read.
# Each entry expires, so Trivy reports it again once the date passes and someone has to
# check whether a fix exists by then. Every other advisory in the root poetry.lock had a
# fixed release and was lifted by floors in pyproject.toml (plan
# 2026-11-05-python-bridge-pillow-and-aiohttp-advisories-are-capped-by-qontinui-core); in
# docker/imagegen, by moving the facade venv to CPython 3.12 and flooring certifi (plan
# 2026-11-05-dependency-advisory-followups-after-the-pillow-13-lift, Phase 5).

# setuptools: torch 2.11.0+cu128 requires setuptools<82, and the cu128 index
# serves no newer torch. The fixes are in 83.0.0 and 84.1.0.
CVE-2026-59890 exp:2027-02-01
GHSA-xmj3-9gf7-h52w exp:2027-02-01

# torch: fixed in 2.13.0, but the pytorch-cu128 index serves only 2.11.0+cu128,
# and torch must stay +cu128.
CVE-2025-3000 exp:2027-02-01
